# Fedora Everything netinstall ISOs scripts/build-iso.sh accepts as input.
# The input ISO's SHA256 must match a line here, or the build stops, so every
# Perihelion ISO is built from a known, unmodified Fedora installer.
#
# Format: <name> <sha256> <url> [<CHECKSUM file url>]
# The last line is the default for --download. With a CHECKSUM file URL,
# --download also checks Fedora's GPG signature on that file (with the
# release key from /etc/pki/rpm-gpg) and that it lists the same SHA256.
#
# To add a release: take the SHA256 from https://fedoraproject.org/misc/
# and its signed CHECKSUM file, then add a line.
#
# 45-1.4: Fedora 45 final (released 2026-11-03). SHA256 as published on
# https://fedoraproject.org/misc/#everything; CI checks the signed CHECKSUM.
45-1.4 42abc36792f91575b2f541db19110cc661864819031e57cd5f5c9ec764ebbddf https://download.fedoraproject.org/pub/fedora/linux/releases/45/Everything/x86_64/iso/Fedora-Everything-netinst-x86_64-45-1.4.iso https://download.fedoraproject.org/pub/fedora/linux/releases/45/Everything/x86_64/iso/Fedora-Everything-45-1.4-x86_64-CHECKSUM
